the captions as an SRT sidecar at\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/references/troubleshooting.md:80:`video_build/captions.srt`. Many players accept that as an external track.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/references/troubleshooting.md:116:To bypass every cache for one run:\n./video_claw/tts/macos.py:12:  * No word-level timing. Callers that need alignment (caption burn) will\n./video_claw/config.py:22:        {\"type\": \"image\", \"image\": \"assets/screenshot.png\", \"narration\": \"...\"},\n./video_claw/config.py:23:        {\"type\": \"video\", \"video\": \"assets/demo.mp4\", \"narration\": \"...\", \"title\": \"Demo\"},\n./video_claw/config.py:37:from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n./video_claw/config.py:57:        \"avatar\": \"assets/avatar.png\",  # relative to project dir; only used on slides with lipsync=True\n./video_claw/config.py:68:    \"captions\": {\n./video_claw/config.py:69:        \"estimate\": True,      # always caption: estimate timing when TTS gives no alignment\n./video_claw/config.py:74:@dataclass\n./video_claw/config.py:75:class Project:\n./video_claw/config.py:102:    # into DEFAULT_CONFIG (or whichever base was passed).\n./video_claw/config.py:138:    config.setdefault(\"captions\", {})[\"estimate\"] = True\n./video_claw/config.py:152:        assert spec.loader is not None\n./video_claw/config.py:181:asset with a string of narration the TTS engine will speak.\n./video_claw/config.py:189:    #                  # every slide, free estimated captions, no paid APIs.\n./video_claw/config.py:205:        \"lipsync\": True,    # uses assets/avatar.png; needs FAL_API_KEY\n./video_claw/tts/__init__.py:6:caption timing. Deepgram and macOS produce no word-level alignment;\n./video_claw/tts/__init__.py:7:caption flow degrades to estimated timing.\n./video_claw/tts/__init__.py:137:    \"\"\"Deepgram Aura-2 TTS → m4a. No timestamp alignment available; captions\n./video_claw/tts/__init__.py:216:    Explicit providers pass through unchanged (the per-provider function still\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:3:description: Use when the user wants to produce a narrated slide video (explainer, demo, walkthrough, short, reel) with AI TTS, optional lip-synced presenter, and burned-in captions. Wraps the `video-claw` CLI. Triggers on phrases like \"make a video about X\", \"turn this into a narrated walkthrough\", \"build a short for Shorts/TikTok/Reels\", \"add narration to these slides\".\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:20:This skill is for slide-based, narrated, captioned videos.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:39:You also need a Chromium-class browser somewhere on disk (Google Chrome,\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:40:Chromium, or Brave). On macOS, Google Chrome is the assumed default. The\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:44:Optional, only if you want captions burned into the MP4 vs the SRT sidecar:\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:48:Stock Homebrew ffmpeg lacks libass, so the burn step falls back to shipping\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:49:an SRT sidecar by default. `imageio-ffmpeg` carries a libass-enabled binary.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:57:| `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` | Default TTS (also drives word-level captions) | https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys |\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:59:| `DEEPGRAM_API_KEY` | Only if `tts.provider=\"deepgram\"` (cheaper, no captions) | https://console.deepgram.com |\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:82:- **Visual assets.** Screenshots, diagrams, app clips. **Ask for real\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:83:  assets.** Do not generate placeholder screenshots. If the user has none,\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:85:  that depend on assets that don't exist.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:87:  `assets/avatar.png`. Flatten the background on solid black before saving;\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:99:starter HTML slides under `slides/`, and the default `assets/avatar.png`.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:109:{\"type\": \"image\", \"image\": \"assets/screenshot.png\",\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:111:{\"type\": \"video\", \"video\": \"assets/clip.mp4\",\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:119:In `slides/`, use the provided `_shared.css` for design tokens. Body class:\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:153:3. Stitches per-slide MP4s, concatenates, burns captions if libass is\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:154:   available (otherwise ships an SRT sidecar).\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:163:To bypass all caches: `FORCE_REGEN=1 video-claw render`.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:169:- **Real assets only.** No placeholder screenshots, no lorem-ipsum diagrams.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:172:  catches typos, broken layouts, and missing assets before the meter runs.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:192:- **Static presenter** — Becky (bundled `assets/avatar.png`) as a circular\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:195:- **Free estimated-timing captions** — burned in locally, no API.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:204:Pin a provider explicitly to force it. Captions are always produced —\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:206:keys still gets a complete captioned video on a Mac; keys only raise quality.\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:210:- **Caption burn fails.** Stock Homebrew ffmpeg lacks libass. Run\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:213:  binary just for the caption step. Until then the package ships an SRT\n./video_claw/skill_data/video-claw/SKILL.md:214:  sidecar at `video_build/captions.srt`.\n./video_claw/cli.py:56:def _assets_dir() -> Path:\n./video_claw/cli.py:57:    return Path(__file__).parent / \"assets\"\n./video_claw/cli.py:68:    assets_dir = target / \"assets\"\n./video_claw/cli.py:70:    for d in (slides_dir, assets_dir, out_dir):\n./video_claw/cli.py:93:    avatar_src = _assets_dir() / \"avatar.png\"\n./video_claw/cli.py:94:    avatar_dst = assets_dir / \"avatar.png\"\n./video_claw/cli.py:207:        pairs = args.assignments\n./video_claw/cli.py:214:                print(f\"error: bad assignment {pair!r} (need NAME=value)\", file=sys.stderr)\n./video_claw/cli.py:326:            captions_cfg=project.config.get(\"captions\"),\n./video_claw/cli.py:405:    pk.add_argument(\"assignments\", nargs=\"*\", help=\"NAME=value pairs (for `set`).\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
